BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20261114T061340Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53640267080597
DTSTART:20261015T180000Z
DTEND:20261015T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Crinoid Fossil Bed Hike at 2:00 p.m.\n•    Sign up at tinyurl
 .com/crinoidhike2026 \n•    Register by October 13.\n•    Limited to 2
 0 people\, recommended for teens and adults.\n•    Location: Allens Cree
 k SRA\nTake a walk back in time to reconstruct what the landscape was like
  here during the Mississippian Period… on this 2-hour hike to a crinoid 
 fossil bed\, we’ll examine what fossils can tell us about the past and h
 ow they form – and why there are so many at this particular location. NO
  COLLECTING PERMITTED. 2 hours. Total distance covered is about 2 miles\, 
 including a couple significant hills.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Allens Creek SRA\, Allens Creek Road\, Bloomington
SUMMARY:ROCKS\, ROCK! Crinoid Fossil Bed Hike\, Allens Creek SRA (Monroe La
 ke)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/rocks-rock-crinoid-fossil-bed-hik
 e-allens-creek-sra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20261114T061340Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53638558906957
DTSTART:20261016T143000Z
DTEND:20261016T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Sand Candles from 10:30 a.m. to 12 p.m.\nPaynetown SRA\, Swimmi
 ng Beach\n\nDROP BY to learn where sand comes from (why does it look diffe
 rent at different beaches?) and sculpt a mold in the beach sand\, which wi
 ll be filled with wax to create a unique candle! Candles must be picked up
  between 1 and 4 p.m. today on the patio at the Activity Center. Suggested
  donation of $2 per candle to help cover supply costs.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Swimming Beach
SUMMARY:ROCKS\, ROCK! Sand Candles\, Paynetown SRA (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/sand-candles-paynetown-sra-monroe
 -lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
