DTSTART:20261023T230000Z
DTEND:20261024T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Halloween Legends Luminary Trail from 7 to 9 p.m.\nPaynetown SR
 A\, Trail begins at front end of Overflow Parking Area (by the trailhead)\
 n\n•    No one will be allowed to begin the trail after 8:30 p.m. \n• 
    The trail closes completely at 9 p.m.\, so make sure you are out of the
  woods by then.\n•    All children under the age of 16 must be accompani
 ed on the trail by an adult.\n•    Please bring a flashlight (make a “
 red light” cover for it at the trail entrance!).\n•    The luminary tr
 ail is included with park admission. A donation box will be at the end of 
 the trail\; if you enjoy it\, please support it!\n\nWind your way through 
 the dark woods along our luminary trail… as you walk\, you can learn abo
 ut the origins of Halloween traditions and monsters – and test your obse
 rvation skills by searching for both “glowing eyes” and pumpkins among
 st the trees. When you emerge from the trail\, enjoy a cup of hot cider an
 d a sweet treat. (If you find all the glowing eyes and pumpkins successful
 ly\, enter the drawing to win a 2027 Indiana State Parks annual entrance p
 ass!)
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA
SUMMARY:GHOSTLY GATHERING: Halloween Legends Luminary Trail\, Paynetown SRA
  (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/ghostly-gathering-halloween-legen
 ds-luminary-trail-paynetown-sra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
