DESCRIPTION:Virtual Program: “What Remains: The Monroe Reservoir Cemetery
  Relocation Project” at 10:00 a.m.\n\nThis program will be presented LIV
 E on Facebook at tinyurl.com/cemeteryrelocation2026\, with a question-and-
 answer session offered at the conclusion of the program. Mark yourself as 
 “going” to receive a reminder about 10 minutes prior to the program’
 s start! If you are unable to view the program live\, a recording will be 
 available on the Reels tab of Monroe Lake’s Facebook page later in the d
 ay.\n\nIn 1960\, the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers (USACE) was tasked with 
 building a reservoir that would impact almost 50\,000 acres in the Salt Cr
 eek Valley of south-central Indiana. This endeavor would necessitate the u
 prooting of thousands of people currently residing on the land. But it was
 n’t just the living that had to be moved.\n\nThis is the story of how 7 
 cemeteries\, consisting of 335 burials\, were disinterred for the construc
 tion of Monroe Lake – and how they were reburied with the intent of pres
 erving both cemetery history and family connections to the Salt Creek Vall
 ey. \n\nPlease note that Monroe Lake has a public Facebook page. This mean
 s that a Facebook account is not required to watch either the live program
  or the recording\; however\, an account is required if you wish to ask qu
 estions or post comments on the video.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, VIRTUAL presentation at http://tinyurl.com/cemeteryr
 elocation2026
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: VIRTUAL PROGRAM - "What Remains: The Monroe Re
 servoir Cemetery Relocation Project" (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-virtual-progr
 am-what-remains-the-monroe-reservoir-cemetery-relocation-project
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
