DTEND:20261107T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Elkinsville History Tour at 1:30 p.m.\n\n•    Sign up at tiny
 url.com/elkinsville2025 \n•    Registration required by November 3.\n•
     Cost is $10 per person.\n•    Limited to 15 people\; recommended for
  ages 14 and up.\n•    Location: Meet at the Story Inn parking lot in St
 ory\, IN\n\nJoin us for a tour through the “town that was!” Prior to t
 he construction of Monroe Lake\, Elkinsville was a center of commerce and 
 community for a remote part of Brown County. Explore the history of this t
 own\, walk its former main street\, visit the cemetery\, and find out what
  happened to this community after the lake went in. 2 hrs 30 min (approx.)
 \n\nAll registrations are final. No refunds will be offered\, unless the t
 our itself is cancelled. You may transfer an existing reservation to anoth
 er person by contacting Jill Vance at jvance@dnr.in.gov at least 2 days pr
 ior to the tour.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Meets at Story Inn parking lot in Story\, IN (ignore
  S.R. 446 address\; directions will be emailed to registered attendees)
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: Elkinsville History Tour (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-elkinsville-h
 istory-tour-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
