UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54028422771879
DTSTART:20261107T230000Z
DTEND:20261108T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Southern Indiana Folk Songs at 6:00 p.m.\n\n•    Free program
  (donations accepted) and free park entry!\n•    Location: Paynetown Sta
 te Recreation Area\, Activity Center\n•    Please note that seating is l
 imited to 25 people\; we don’t expect the room to fill\, but we could al
 ways be surprised!\n\nFolk songs proliferated in an era when singing was a
  common form of recreation. People learned traditional folk songs by liste
 ning to others sing them and then passing them on to someone else. The Sal
 t Creek Valley\, where Monroe Lake now lies\, has a rich history of song\,
  heavily influenced by the people who moved here in the 1800s from the App
 alachian region. This program explores the history of folk music in southe
 rn Indiana and songs once sung right here in the valley\, including audio 
 recordings of local singers from the 1930s through 1980s.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Activity Center
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: Southern Indiana Folk Songs\, Paynetown SRA (M
 onroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-southern-indi
 ana-folk-songs-paynetown-sra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
